      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-17T09:30:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that we need to create a HandlerThread anyway, why not require that the app pass in a Handler thread? In case the app already has a Handler, that allows us to have one fewer threads, saving memory.\n\nNot for this patch series, but maybe add a TODO?\n\nIf you end up implementing Nathan\u0027s suggestion and use ConnectivityThread directly, then you can just do that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 104,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 104,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "138a1fa5a7f5672ccc243272624fd1e1e87dbdbf",
